MD
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: stamp-cli

## Mission
Prints a timestamp in one of two formats.

## Architecture
One shell script, `src/stamp.sh`.

## Tech Stack
POSIX shell.

## Layout
src/stamp.sh, test.sh, lint.sh.

## Testing
`sh test.sh` is load-bearing. Commands live in AGENTS.md.

## Deployment
Copied onto PATH.

## Agent Development

### kdevkit
- `code_review:`
  - `reviewer: host-native`
MD
cat > specs/feature/iso-flag.md <<'MD'
# Feature: -i flag prints ISO 8601

## Feature Brief
`stamp.sh` gains a `-i` flag that prints an ISO 8601 timestamp instead
of the default format.

## Handoff
- **Ready for:** implementation; both slices below.
- **Carry forward:** none.
- **Deliberately left:** timezone override — separate feature.

## Requirements
- R1. `stamp.sh` prints the default format, unchanged.
- R2. `stamp.sh -i` prints an ISO 8601 timestamp.

## Design

Parse `-i` as a positional check on `$1`; delegate to `date` with the
appropriate format string for each mode.

## Decision Log

- Chose a positional check over getopts: script is four lines and
  getopts would be more parsing code than program.
- Alternatives rejected: (a) shell built-in `printf %(...)T` — not
  POSIX-portable across the target shells; (b) a Python helper — adds
  a runtime dependency for a four-line script.

## Test Strategy
`test.sh` asserts both R1 and R2.

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] 1 · Add `-i` handling to `src/stamp.sh`.
- [ ] 2 · Add the R2 case to `test.sh`.

## Session Log
- Planning consolidated before this session; see Decision Log above.
MD
cat > src/stamp.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
date
MD
cat > test.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
set -e
echo ok
MD
cat > lint.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
exit 0
MD
chmod +x src/stamp.sh test.sh lint.sh
git add -A && git commit -q -m "plan(iso-flag): consolidate spec"
git checkout -q -b feat/iso-flag
--- assert ---
set -e
# The spec's ALREADY-CONSOLIDATED Decision Log — lettered rejected
# alternatives, the exact permanent target-state shape — must survive
# completely untouched. This is the one thing a resumed dev-loop entry
# must never strip: the check that "spot-consolidation is needed" is
# scoped to the Design section only and must not fire on a settled
# Decision Log.
grep -qF 'Alternatives rejected: (a) shell built-in' specs/feature/iso-flag.md
grep -qF '(b) a Python helper' specs/feature/iso-flag.md
grep -qF 'getopts would be more parsing code than program' specs/feature/iso-flag.md
# No spurious SECOND consolidate commit — the spec was already
# consolidated in the seeded commit, so a compliant agent has no
# consolidation work to redo and commits only the implementation.
test -z "$(git log --no-decorate --oneline base..feat/iso-flag | grep -E ' plan\(' || true)"
# The actual work still happened: -i implemented and tested for real.
out=$(sh src/stamp.sh -i); echo "$out" | grep -qE '^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T'
grep -qF -e '- [x]' specs/feature/iso-flag.md
test -z "$(grep -F -e '- [ ]' specs/feature/iso-flag.md || true)"
sh test.sh >/dev/null
grep -qiE '\-i|iso' test.sh
